.TH ABDNSD 8 "November 2026" "abdns 0.2.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
abdnsd \- encrypted DNS client of this computer, with captive portal support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B abdnsd
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-system ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B abdnsd
listens on 127.0.0.1:53 and [::1]:53 and points the system DNS to itself. Every query goes over
DNS-over-HTTPS (RFC 8484) to the configured servers, tried in order: a failing server is set
aside for 30 seconds, up to 5 minutes, and checked again every 30 seconds. Answers are cached
for their lifetime; when no server answers, the last known answer is served for up to one day
(RFC 8767).
.PP
Names of the local network (\fI.local\fR, \fI.lan\fR, \fI.home.arpa\fR, the DHCP domain,
single-label names, reverse lookups of private addresses) always go to the network DNS and are
never reported.
.PP
When every server fails twice in a row while the network DNS answers \(em a captive portal, or a
network blocking encrypted DNS \(em and \fBlocal_fallback\fR is true, abdnsd uses the network
DNS, opens the portal sign-in page if there is one, reports the names sent in clear, and switches
back as soon as an encrypted server answers. A DNSSEC failure never triggers this switch.
.PP
The configuration file is read again whenever it changes; an invalid file is reported and the
previous configuration stays in use. When abdnsd stops or crashes, the system DNS is set back to
the network's.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Configuration file (default: see
.BR abdns (1)).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-system
Do not change the system DNS (testing, with \fBlisten\fR on a port above 1024).
.SH CONFIGURATION
TOML. Only \fB[[server]]\fR is required.
.TP
.B language
\fB"en"\fR or \fB"fr"\fR, for notifications.
.TP
.B local_fallback
Use the network DNS when no server answers (default \fBtrue\fR).
.TP
.B listen
Addresses to listen on (default 127.0.0.1:53 and [::1]:53; restart to change).
.TP
.B [[server]]
\fBname\fR; \fBurl\fR, the DoH URL; \fBip\fR, required when the URL uses a host name, so that
the server is reached without any plaintext lookup; \fBtoken_file\fR, a root-only file whose
content is appended to \fBurl\fR (which then ends with \fB/\fR).
.TP
.B network_services
macOS network services whose DNS points to abdnsd (default \fB["Wi-Fi"]\fR). Ignored on Linux, where abdnsd takes over the physical interfaces the computer goes out by.
.TP
.BR state_dir ", " clear_log
State directory (default \fI/var/run/abdns\fR) and log of names sent in clear (default
\fI/var/log/abdns/clear.log\fR).
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
language = "en"
local_fallback = true

[[server]]
name = "Google"
url = "https://8.8.8.8/dns-query"

[[server]]
name = "Cloudflare"
url = "https://1.1.1.1/dns-query"
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/run/abdns/control.sock
Control socket, group of the administrators, used by
.BR abdns (1).
.TP
.I /var/log/abdns/abdns.log
Service log on macOS (journald on Linux).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR abdns (1)
